window.__READMES["unuMCP"]="<div id=\"readme\" class=\"md\" data-path=\"README.md\"><article class=\"markdown-body entry-content container-lg\" itemprop=\"text\"><div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h1 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">unuMCP</h1><a id=\"user-content-unumcp\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: unuMCP\" href=\"#unumcp\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://aimunna.me/unuMCP/\" rel=\"nofollow\"><img src=\"https://camo.githubusercontent.com/5e2a836fb89ef4a6c8acb1fb3a3dc2fedf8e5569d0389e7bd5476b29485e9d0b/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f62616467652f2545322539372538462532304c69766525323064656d6f2d726571756573742532306163636573732d3265376433323f7374796c653d666f722d7468652d6261646765\" alt=\"Live demo: request access\" data-canonical-src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/%E2%97%8F%20Live%20demo-request%20access-2e7d32?style=for-the-badge\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"></a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Turn an <strong>OpenAPI specification</strong> into a working, tested <strong>TypeScript MCP server</strong>, with a human approval step, a deterministic code generator, a sandboxed test run, and a bounded self-repair loop.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">You upload a spec; unuMCP analyses the endpoints, proposes tools (names, input schemas, risk levels), lets you approve them, generates a complete MCP server project, runs its tests in an isolated Docker sandbox, repairs failing code, and hands back a downloadable ZIP with the README and <code>.env.example</code> included, and no secrets.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/atikulmunna/unuMCP/HEAD/assets/unumcp.png\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/atikulmunna/unuMCP/HEAD/assets/unumcp.png\" alt=\"unuMCP dashboard: the project build pipeline\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"></a></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The project workbench: a five-stage build pipeline (left), the validated spec with <strong>auto-detected bearer auth</strong>, and the approved <strong>tool plan</strong> whose descriptions were authored live by the LLM. Captured from a live AWS deploy (see <a href=\"#deployment\">Deployment</a>).</p>\n</blockquote>\n<hr>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">Table of contents</h2><a id=\"user-content-table-of-contents\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Table of contents\" href=\"#table-of-contents\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"#live-demo\">Live demo</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#how-it-works\">How it works</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#architecture\">Architecture</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#repository-layout\">Repository layout</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#prerequisites\">Prerequisites</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#quick-start\">Quick start</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#environment-variables\">Environment variables</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#running-the-apps\">Running the apps</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#testing\">Testing</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#observability\">Observability</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#security-posture\">Security posture</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#deployment\">Deployment</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#operational-notes\">Operational notes</a></li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">Live demo</h2><a id=\"user-content-live-demo\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Live demo\" href=\"#live-demo\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The demo runs on an <strong>on-demand</strong> cloud box that is <strong>kept switched off to keep hosting costs near zero</strong>, so there is deliberately no always-on public URL (see <a href=\"#deployment\">Deployment</a> for why: it needs a real Docker daemon for the sandbox, which isn't free to run 24/7).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Want to see it live?</strong> Open the <strong><a href=\"https://aimunna.me/unuMCP/\" rel=\"nofollow\">live-demo page</a></strong> (that's where the badge above goes), or reach out directly and the author will spin the server up (~30 seconds) and send you a URL, then take it down again afterwards:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>📧 <strong>Atikul Munna</strong>: <a href=\"mailto:atikul.munna@northsouth.edu?subject=unuMCP%20live%20demo%20request\">atikul.munna@northsouth.edu</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">In the meantime, the <a href=\"#unumcp\">screenshot above</a> and <a href=\"#how-it-works\">How it works</a> walk through the entire pipeline.</p>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">How it works</h2><a id=\"user-content-how-it-works\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: How it works\" href=\"#how-it-works\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The platform is a <strong>deterministic pipeline with one human gate</strong>, not an open-ended agent loop. Each stage advances a <code>Project</code> through an auditable state machine (every transition writes a <code>GenerationRun</code> status + an <code>AuditEvent</code>).</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"Upload OpenAPI spec\n  → validate + dereference ($ref / allOf / oneOf)\n  → analyse endpoints → propose tools (deterministic name + risk + input schema;\n                                       optional LLM-authored descriptions, and an\n                                       LLM risk rating that can only raise risk)\n  → optional: agent usability check  (an LLM agent tries each tool; fixes to review)\n  → 👤 human approval  (high-risk tools disabled by default)\n  → generate TypeScript MCP server  (deterministic codegen, with a runtime\n                                     safety policy: approval, dry run, read-only)\n  → static security scan  (refuse code that smells of secrets / exfiltration / eval)\n  → run tests in a locked-down Docker sandbox  (deps prebuilt into the image, test offline)\n  → on failure: bounded self-repair loop  (fix implementation only, tests frozen)\n  → complete → download ZIP  (sources + tests + README + .env.example, no secrets)\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code>Upload OpenAPI spec\n  → validate + dereference ($ref / allOf / oneOf)\n  → analyse endpoints → propose tools (deterministic name + risk + input schema;\n                                       optional LLM-authored descriptions, and an\n                                       LLM risk rating that can only raise risk)\n  → optional: agent usability check  (an LLM agent tries each tool; fixes to review)\n  → 👤 human approval  (high-risk tools disabled by default)\n  → generate TypeScript MCP server  (deterministic codegen, with a runtime\n                                     safety policy: approval, dry run, read-only)\n  → static security scan  (refuse code that smells of secrets / exfiltration / eval)\n  → run tests in a locked-down Docker sandbox  (deps prebuilt into the image, test offline)\n  → on failure: bounded self-repair loop  (fix implementation only, tests frozen)\n  → complete → download ZIP  (sources + tests + README + .env.example, no secrets)\n</code></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Design principles worth knowing before you read the code:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><strong>Determinism first.</strong> All <em>structural</em> artifacts (project scaffold, handler wiring, env detection, tests) are generated deterministically. The LLM is used <strong>only</strong> for prose (tool descriptions) and for repair edits, never to produce structural code. The platform runs end-to-end with the LLM disabled (you just get fallback descriptions and no repair).</li>\n<li><strong>The LLM is Claude, and opt-in.</strong> <code>@unumcp/llm</code> wraps Anthropic's official SDK (default Claude Haiku 4.5) behind a small <code>LlmClient</code> interface, so tests drive every LLM stage with a scripted client. It bills per token, so it runs only when explicitly turned on. Descriptions are proposed in <strong>batches</strong> (many tools per call) to keep the token cost of a large spec down. See <a href=\"#environment-variables\">Environment variables</a>.</li>\n<li><strong>Generated tests check the contract, not just that code runs.</strong> Each tool is called through a real MCP client (in-memory transport) with the API stubbed, and its test asserts the exact HTTP request the spec defines: method, path, query (OpenAPI's default serialization), headers, auth, and body encoding. It also checks that the response reaches the agent unchanged, that API errors become tool errors, and that calls missing required inputs are rejected. The sandbox typechecks the server before running them. Injected bugs (wrong path, a dropped header or auth, a misencoded body, swallowed errors) all fail.</li>\n<li><strong>Tools are tested on an agent before you approve them.</strong> An on-demand check has an LLM play the agent: for up to 40 tools, most easily confused first, it gets a realistic request, written from the spec with each tool's real endpoint in view, and must pick the right tool, among the target and its closest look-alikes, with the right arguments. The agent sees only what an MCP client sees (names, descriptions, inputs). For each miss it proposes clearer tool text; when the agent picked the wrong tool, both tools of the confused pair are rewritten together, grounded in their endpoints and inputs. A fix is offered only if re-scoring shows it turns the miss into a hit without breaking another tool. You accept or reject each fix, and see the score before and after (for example 8 of 9, then 9 of 9) with the check's cost. Nothing generated is executed: the model only sees tool metadata. It needs the LLM; a 9-tool check costs about $0.03 on Claude Haiku 4.5, growing with the number of tools checked.</li>\n<li><strong>Large APIs stay reviewable.</strong> Tools are grouped by the spec's tags (GitHub's 1,209 tools fall into 47 groups). Long plans are shown by group, with a search and a switch per group; turning a group on leaves its high and critical tools off. The groups carry into the generated server as toolsets, so <code>MCP_TOOLSETS=issues,pulls</code> exposes just those groups at runtime.</li>\n<li><strong>A sample project shows the check without an API key.</strong> \"Try a sample\" on the projects page creates the Acme Billing sample: a small spec whose look-alike routes (all invoices with a status filter, and a separate drafts route) confuse an agent, the way many real specs do. Its usability check ran once with Claude and was recorded (<code>apps/api/src/samples/acme-billing.recorded.ts</code>), so creating a sample makes no LLM calls, while the rest of the pipeline runs live. After changing the sample spec or the check, refresh the recording with <code>apps/api/scripts/record-sample.mts</code> (its header explains how; it costs a few cents).</li>\n<li><strong>Risk is enforced at runtime, not just shown at approval.</strong> Risk comes from rules (method, sensitive nouns, and action words a method hides, such as <code>merge</code> or <code>transfer</code>); the LLM may rate a tool riskier, never safer, and a raise is audited. Every generated server carries the result: MCP behavior hints (<code>readOnlyHint</code>, <code>destructiveHint</code>, <code>idempotentHint</code>) on each tool, and a policy set by environment variables (<code>MCP_READ_ONLY</code>, <code>MCP_TOOLSETS</code>, <code>MCP_ENABLED_TOOLS</code>, <code>MCP_DISABLED_TOOLS</code>, <code>MCP_DRY_RUN</code>, <code>MCP_CONFIRM_RISK</code>). By default a high or critical tool runs only after the user approves the exact request through MCP elicitation; a client that can't ask gets a refusal, not a silent call. The generated tests prove each path (approve, decline, no elicitation support, dry run, read-only filtering), and removing any guard fails them.</li>\n<li><strong>Tests are frozen during repair.</strong> The repair loop may edit <code>src/**/*.ts</code> only: tests, <code>package.json</code>, and <code>tsconfig.json</code> are never offered to the model, and the parser rejects any other path. Every repair passes the same security scan as generated code before it is applied, and a run only counts as passing when at least one test reports a pass, so an edit can't win by making the suite run nothing.</li>\n<li><strong>Every internal LLM call is traced.</strong> Each agent tool call (<code>propose_tool_descriptions_batch</code>, <code>repair_code</code>) is recorded as an audit event with token counts, and its cost rolls up into per-run and platform metrics, with secrets redacted throughout.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">Architecture</h2><a id=\"user-content-architecture\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Architecture\" href=\"#architecture\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<markdown-accessiblity-table><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Layer</th>\n<th>Tech</th>\n<th>Notes</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Language</td>\n<td><strong>TypeScript 6</strong> throughout</td>\n<td>The API and its packages compile ahead of time with SWC; dev runs from source</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Backend / orchestrator</td>\n<td><strong>NestJS 12</strong></td>\n<td>DI + guards map cleanly to the auth/authz and multi-stage layout</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Frontend dashboard</td>\n<td><strong>Next.js 16</strong> (App Router), React 19, Tailwind v4</td>\n<td>Same-origin <code>/api/*</code> proxied to the backend (no CORS needed)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Database</td>\n<td><strong>PostgreSQL 16</strong> via <strong>Prisma 7</strong> (pg driver adapter)</td>\n<td>Projects, runs, tools, test results, repair attempts, audit log</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Background jobs</td>\n<td><strong>BullMQ + Redis</strong> (optional)</td>\n<td>Long-running generation/test/repair survive restarts; falls back to inline</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sandbox</td>\n<td><strong>Docker</strong>, prebuilt image</td>\n<td>Dependencies baked into a content-hashed image; tests run with <code>--network none</code>, non-root, no capabilities, read-only mounts, resource caps</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>LLM</td>\n<td><strong>Anthropic Claude</strong> (official SDK), via <code>@unumcp/llm</code></td>\n<td>Opt-in (<code>LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic</code>); optional, since the platform degrades gracefully without it</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Generated servers</td>\n<td><strong>TypeScript 6</strong>, <strong>MCP SDK 1.32.1</strong>, <strong>Zod 4</strong>, <strong>Vitest 5</strong> (Node 22.12+)</td>\n<td>One dependency set for every server, baked into the sandbox image</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Testing</td>\n<td><strong>Vitest 5</strong>, <strong>Playwright</strong></td>\n<td>Unit and API suites against real Postgres, plus a browser smoke test of the production build in CI</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Monorepo</td>\n<td><strong>pnpm workspaces + Turborepo</strong></td>\n<td>Shared <code>packages/*</code>, cached <code>build</code>/<code>test</code>/<code>typecheck</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">Repository layout</h2><a id=\"user-content-repository-layout\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Repository layout\" href=\"#repository-layout\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"apps/\n  api/      NestJS backend: REST API + the pipeline orchestrator, jobs, sandbox, repair\n  web/      Next.js dashboard: spec upload, tool approval, pipeline progress, downloads\npackages/\n  openapi/        Parse/validate OpenAPI, dereference $ref/allOf/oneOf, extract endpoints, detect auth\n  analysis/       Endpoint → tool classification, deterministic naming, risk scoring, proposal assembly\n  usability/      Agent usability check logic: look-alike selection, target picking, answer scoring\n  schema-gen/     JSON Schema → Zod input-schema generation\n  codegen/        Deterministic TypeScript MCP server generation (project, handlers, tests, README, .env.example)\n  sandbox/        Docker sandbox: prebuilt dependency image, locked-down test runner, Vitest summary parser\n  security-scan/  Secret redaction, static scan of generated code, prompt-injection detection\n  llm/            Claude client (Anthropic SDK): tool descriptions, code repair, usability prompts\n  db/             Prisma schema + generated client\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code>apps/\n  api/      NestJS backend: REST API + the pipeline orchestrator, jobs, sandbox, repair\n  web/      Next.js dashboard: spec upload, tool approval, pipeline progress, downloads\npackages/\n  openapi/        Parse/validate OpenAPI, dereference $ref/allOf/oneOf, extract endpoints, detect auth\n  analysis/       Endpoint → tool classification, deterministic naming, risk scoring, proposal assembly\n  usability/      Agent usability check logic: look-alike selection, target picking, answer scoring\n  schema-gen/     JSON Schema → Zod input-schema generation\n  codegen/        Deterministic TypeScript MCP server generation (project, handlers, tests, README, .env.example)\n  sandbox/        Docker sandbox: prebuilt dependency image, locked-down test runner, Vitest summary parser\n  security-scan/  Secret redaction, static scan of generated code, prompt-injection detection\n  llm/            Claude client (Anthropic SDK): tool descriptions, code repair, usability prompts\n  db/             Prisma schema + generated client\n</code></pre></div>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Note on untracked docs:</strong> <code>unuMCP_SRS.md</code>, <code>tasks.md</code>, and <code>CLAUDE.md</code> are intentionally git-ignored (local planning/spec docs). This README is the canonical project documentation; <a href=\"ARCHITECTURE.md\">ARCHITECTURE.md</a> covers the design: pipeline, key decisions, trust boundaries, and what the requirement tags in code comments mean.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">Prerequisites</h2><a id=\"user-content-prerequisites\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Prerequisites\" href=\"#prerequisites\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><strong>Node.js ≥ 22.19</strong> (required by swagger-parser 13, the spec dereferencer)</li>\n<li><strong>pnpm 11.5.1</strong> (<code>corepack enable</code> will pin it from <code>packageManager</code>)</li>\n<li><strong>Docker</strong>: required both for local Postgres/Redis (<code>docker compose</code>) <strong>and</strong> for the test sandbox that runs a generated server's tests</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">Quick start</h2><a id=\"user-content-quick-start\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Quick start\" href=\"#quick-start\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-shell notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"# 1. Install workspace deps (generates the Prisma client on postinstall)\npnpm install\n\n# 2. Start Postgres (:5433) and Redis (:6379)\ndocker compose up -d\n\n# 3. Configure env for the API\ncp .env.example apps/api/.env\n#   then edit apps/api/.env; at minimum set DATABASE_URL and JWT_SECRET\n#   (REDIS_URL and the LLM, LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic plus ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, are optional; see below)\n\n# 4. Apply the database schema.\n#   The Prisma CLI reads DATABASE_URL from the environment (NOT apps/api/.env;\n#   see packages/db/prisma.config.ts), so pass it for the docker-compose database:\nDATABASE_URL=postgresql://unumcp:unumcp@localhost:5433/unumcp \\\n  pnpm --filter @unumcp/db exec prisma migrate deploy\n\n# 5. Run the backend (http://localhost:3001/api)\npnpm --filter @unumcp/api dev\n\n# 6. In another terminal, run the dashboard (http://localhost:3000)\npnpm --filter @unumcp/web dev\"><pre><span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> 1. Install workspace deps (generates the Prisma client on postinstall)</span>\npnpm install\n\n<span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> 2. Start Postgres (:5433) and Redis (:6379)</span>\ndocker compose up -d\n\n<span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> 3. Configure env for the API</span>\ncp .env.example apps/api/.env\n<span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span>   then edit apps/api/.env; at minimum set DATABASE_URL and JWT_SECRET</span>\n<span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span>   (REDIS_URL and the LLM, LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic plus ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, are optional; see below)</span>\n\n<span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> 4. Apply the database schema.</span>\n<span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span>   The Prisma CLI reads DATABASE_URL from the environment (NOT apps/api/.env;</span>\n<span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span>   see packages/db/prisma.config.ts), so pass it for the docker-compose database:</span>\nDATABASE_URL=postgresql://unumcp:unumcp@localhost:5433/unumcp \\\n  pnpm --filter @unumcp/db <span class=\"pl-c1\">exec</span> prisma migrate deploy\n\n<span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> 5. Run the backend (http://localhost:3001/api)</span>\npnpm --filter @unumcp/api dev\n\n<span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> 6. In another terminal, run the dashboard (http://localhost:3000)</span>\npnpm --filter @unumcp/web dev</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Open <a href=\"http://localhost:3000\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://localhost:3000</a>, register an account, create a project, and upload an OpenAPI spec to start the pipeline.</p>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">Environment variables</h2><a id=\"user-content-environment-variables\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Environment variables\" href=\"#environment-variables\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The API loads <code>apps/api/.env</code> (via Node's <code>--env-file</code>). Copy <code>.env.example</code> and adjust. All keys:</p>\n<markdown-accessiblity-table><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Variable</th>\n<th>Required</th>\n<th>Default</th>\n<th>Purpose</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>DATABASE_URL</code></td>\n<td><strong>yes</strong></td>\n<td><code>postgresql://unumcp:unumcp@localhost:5433/unumcp</code></td>\n<td>Postgres connection (Prisma)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>JWT_SECRET</code></td>\n<td><strong>yes</strong></td>\n<td>none: the API refuses to start without it</td>\n<td>Signs/verifies auth tokens. At least 32 characters (<code>openssl rand -hex 32</code>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>PORT</code></td>\n<td>no</td>\n<td><code>3001</code></td>\n<td>API listen port</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>LLM_PROVIDER</code></td>\n<td>no</td>\n<td>(none)</td>\n<td>Set to <code>anthropic</code> to turn the LLM on; it also needs <code>ANTHROPIC_API_KEY</code>. A key alone never starts billing. <strong>Off ⇒ deterministic fallback, no repair</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ANTHROPIC_API_KEY</code></td>\n<td>no</td>\n<td>(none)</td>\n<td>Anthropic key, used only with <code>LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ANTHROPIC_MODEL</code></td>\n<td>no</td>\n<td><code>claude-haiku-4-5</code></td>\n<td>Claude model id, e.g. <code>claude-sonnet-5-5</code> or <code>claude-opus-5-5</code>. Cost appears in run metrics and <code>/metrics</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>LLM_DISABLED</code></td>\n<td>no</td>\n<td>(none)</td>\n<td>Set <code>true</code> to force-disable the LLM even when configured</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>PROPOSAL_BATCH_SIZE</code></td>\n<td>no</td>\n<td><code>5</code></td>\n<td>Tools described per LLM call (batched proposal, P2-6)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>PROPOSAL_CONCURRENCY</code></td>\n<td>no</td>\n<td><code>3</code></td>\n<td>Description batches in flight at once</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>USABILITY_MAX_TASKS</code></td>\n<td>no</td>\n<td><code>40</code></td>\n<td>Tasks per agent usability check (one per tested tool)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>USABILITY_CONCURRENCY</code></td>\n<td>no</td>\n<td><code>2</code></td>\n<td>Agent calls in flight during a check</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>USABILITY_MAX_CALLS</code></td>\n<td>no</td>\n<td><code>150</code></td>\n<td>Hard ceiling on LLM calls per check; the run fails beyond it</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>REDIS_URL</code></td>\n<td>no</td>\n<td>(none)</td>\n<td><strong>Absent ⇒ jobs run inline.</strong> Set to enable the durable BullMQ queue</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>JOBS_INLINE</code></td>\n<td>no</td>\n<td>(none)</td>\n<td>Set <code>true</code> to force inline execution even with <code>REDIS_URL</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>JOB_ATTEMPTS</code></td>\n<td>no</td>\n<td><code>3</code></td>\n<td>BullMQ retry attempts per job</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>JOB_CONCURRENCY</code></td>\n<td>no</td>\n<td><code>2</code></td>\n<td>Worker concurrency</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>MAX_REPAIR_ATTEMPTS</code></td>\n<td>no</td>\n<td><code>2</code></td>\n<td>Bounded self-repair passes (each ≈ one LLM call + a full sandbox rerun)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>REPAIR_MAX_TOKENS</code></td>\n<td>no</td>\n<td><code>4096</code></td>\n<td>Token ceiling per repair pass</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>SANDBOX_CONCURRENCY</code></td>\n<td>no</td>\n<td><code>1</code></td>\n<td>Sandbox runs (tests and repair reruns) allowed at once; further runs queue</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>RATE_LIMIT_MAX</code></td>\n<td>no</td>\n<td><code>60</code></td>\n<td>Requests per window</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW_MS</code></td>\n<td>no</td>\n<td><code>60000</code></td>\n<td>Rate-limit window</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>RATE_LIMIT_DISABLED</code></td>\n<td>no</td>\n<td>(none)</td>\n<td>Set <code>true</code> to disable rate limiting</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>STORAGE_DIR</code></td>\n<td>no</td>\n<td>OS temp dir</td>\n<td>Where generated artifacts are stored locally</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The <strong>web</strong> app honours <code>API_URL</code> (default <code>http://localhost:3001</code>) for the Next rewrite that proxies <code>/api/*</code> to the backend.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Secrets never leave the platform.</strong> Generated archives contain only <code>.env.example</code> placeholders, never a populated <code>.env</code>. Secret-shaped values are redacted from logs and error messages.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">Running the apps</h2><a id=\"user-content-running-the-apps\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Running the apps\" href=\"#running-the-apps\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Backend.</strong> Start it with the workspace script:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-shell notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"pnpm --filter @unumcp/api dev                     # watch mode, straight from TypeScript\npnpm exec turbo run build --filter=@unumcp/api... # compile the API and its packages\npnpm --filter @unumcp/api start                   # run the compiled build (as production does)\"><pre>pnpm --filter @unumcp/api dev                     <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> watch mode, straight from TypeScript</span>\npnpm <span class=\"pl-c1\">exec</span> turbo run build --filter=@unumcp/api... <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> compile the API and its packages</span>\npnpm --filter @unumcp/api start                   <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> run the compiled build (as production does)</span></pre></div>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><g-emoji class=\"g-emoji\" alias=\"warning\">⚠️</g-emoji> <code>dev</code> runs under <code>node -r @swc-node/register</code>, <strong>not</strong> <code>tsx</code>: NestJS needs <code>emitDecoratorMetadata</code> for constructor DI, and SWC emits it while esbuild/tsx does not. The build (<code>scripts/swc-build.mjs</code>) uses the same SWC transform, writing each package's <code>dist/</code>; <code>start</code> runs it with <code>node -C unumcp-dist</code>, the export condition that points the workspace packages at their <code>dist/</code> instead of their TypeScript source.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Dashboard.</strong> Start the API first (it needs Postgres), then:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-shell notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"pnpm --filter @unumcp/web dev     # Next dev on :3000, proxies /api → :3001\"><pre>pnpm --filter @unumcp/web dev     <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> Next dev on :3000, proxies /api → :3001</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The browser keeps the JWT in <code>localStorage</code> and calls same-origin <code>/api/*</code>; Next rewrites proxy those to the backend, so the API needs no CORS configuration.</p>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">Testing</h2><a id=\"user-content-testing\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Testing\" href=\"#testing\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-shell notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"pnpm test          # all packages via Turborepo\npnpm typecheck     # tsc --noEmit across the workspace\npnpm lint          # ESLint (typescript-eslint + React hooks) over the whole repo\"><pre>pnpm <span class=\"pl-c1\">test</span>          <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> all packages via Turborepo</span>\npnpm typecheck     <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> tsc --noEmit across the workspace</span>\npnpm lint          <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> ESLint (typescript-eslint + React hooks) over the whole repo</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Per package / app:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-shell notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"pnpm exec turbo run typecheck test --filter=@unumcp/llm\npnpm exec turbo run typecheck test build --filter=@unumcp/web\"><pre>pnpm <span class=\"pl-c1\">exec</span> turbo run typecheck <span class=\"pl-c1\">test</span> --filter=@unumcp/llm\npnpm <span class=\"pl-c1\">exec</span> turbo run typecheck <span class=\"pl-c1\">test</span> build --filter=@unumcp/web</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Notes:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><strong>The API test suite needs a Postgres with the schema applied</strong> (it exercises real Prisma against <code>DATABASE_URL</code>). Bring up <code>docker compose</code> and run <code>prisma migrate deploy</code> first.</li>\n<li><strong>Schema changes need a migration.</strong> After editing <code>packages/db/prisma/schema.prisma</code>, run <code>pnpm --filter @unumcp/db exec prisma migrate dev --name &lt;what-changed&gt;</code> and commit the new folder under <code>prisma/migrations/</code>. CI applies the migrations to an empty database and fails if the result differs from the schema.</li>\n<li>The <strong>browser smoke test</strong> (<code>pnpm --filter @unumcp/web e2e</code>, Playwright, runs in CI) builds the web app for production, starts it and the API on ports 3100 and 3101, and drives Chromium through sign-up, a new project, a spec upload and a tool plan. It also checks the stylesheets and web fonts load. It needs the same Postgres; run <code>pnpm --filter @unumcp/web exec playwright install chromium</code> once.</li>\n<li>The <strong>real-Redis queue round-trip</strong> test is opt-in: it only runs when <code>REDIS_URL</code> is set (the default suite runs jobs inline).</li>\n<li>The <strong>real Docker sandbox</strong> is covered by an opt-in suite: <code>RUN_SANDBOX_DOCKER_TESTS=1 pnpm --filter @unumcp/api exec vitest run tests/sandbox.security.e2e.test.ts</code> proves, from inside a container, that there is no network, no root, and no write access to the project or the image, plus timeout cleanup and log redaction. Other unit/e2e tests use an injectable fake sandbox so they don't require Docker. The first real run builds the sandbox image (<code>pnpm --filter @unumcp/sandbox build-image</code> pre-builds it).</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">Observability</h2><a id=\"user-content-observability\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Observability\" href=\"#observability\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Two dependency-free surfaces (the JSON shapes are drop-in for a real shipper later):</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><strong>Structured request logs + trace ids.</strong> One JSON line per HTTP request (<code>requestId</code>, method, path, status, <code>durationMs</code>); errors carry a <code>correlationId</code> that links the client envelope to the server log.</li>\n<li><strong>Metrics</strong> at <code>GET /metrics</code> (JWT-scoped to the caller): projects created, specs parsed, servers generated, generation success rate, test pass rate, average generation time, repair counts, failed sandbox runs, and <strong>LLM cost</strong> (<code>totalInputTokens</code> / <code>totalOutputTokens</code> / <code>totalEstimatedCostUsd</code>).</li>\n<li><strong>Per-call LLM trace (FR-031).</strong> Every internal agent tool call is an <code>llm_tool_call</code> audit event carrying an input/output summary, token counts, latency, and any error, all secret-redacted. Proposal and repair token usage rolls up onto the <code>GenerationRun</code> and into the metrics cost, priced per model from Claude's list prices.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">Security posture</h2><a id=\"user-content-security-posture\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Security posture\" href=\"#security-posture\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><strong>Human approval gate</strong> before any code is generated; high and critical tools (deletes, admin and auth endpoints, and irreversible actions like <code>merge</code> or <code>transfer</code>) are disabled by default.</li>\n<li><strong>Runtime approval in the generated server</strong>: risky calls wait for the user's approval through MCP elicitation, and the server can be limited to read-only tools, chosen toolsets, an allow list, or dry runs (see the generated README's \"Safety controls\").</li>\n<li><strong>Static security scan</strong> of generated code and of every LLM repair before it is persisted or packaged: refuses injected secrets, exfiltration hosts, and <code>eval</code>/shell patterns. Code is read through the TypeScript parser, so documentation (comments, tool and field descriptions) isn't mistaken for behaviour; that agent-facing text gets its own check: the API's own docs links pass, other links are noted for review, and an instruction to send data to an outside host is refused (tool poisoning).</li>\n<li><strong>Locked-down sandbox, no install step</strong>: every generated server declares the same dependency set, so it is baked into a prebuilt, content-hashed image and nothing is downloaded or installed at test time (a project declaring anything else is refused before any container starts). Tests run as the image's own Vitest (never a project <code>npm</code> script) with <code>--network none</code>, a non-root user, all capabilities dropped, <code>no-new-privileges</code>, CPU/memory/pid caps, a read-only root FS, and the project mounted read-only. Runs are serialized (<code>SANDBOX_CONCURRENCY</code>), and a timeout or cancel force-removes the container through the Docker daemon.</li>\n<li><strong>No default signing key</strong>: the API will not boot without a <code>JWT_SECRET</code> of at least 32 characters, and it signs and accepts HS256 tokens only.</li>\n<li><strong>Uploaded specs can't reach the server</strong>: a <code>$ref</code> to another file or a URL is refused at upload and never followed (it would make the server read its own files or fetch URLs), a server URL with spaces or line breaks is refused (it would add lines to the generated <code>.env.example</code>), and an upload's file name can't contain folders.</li>\n<li><strong>Prompt-injection detection</strong> on untrusted spec text feeding the LLM; the description prompt treats spec content as untrusted data.</li>\n<li><strong>Secret redaction</strong> across logs, error envelopes, and persisted sandbox output.</li>\n<li><strong>Sanitized error responses</strong>: a single exception filter returns a structured envelope with a correlation id; 5xx bodies are generic (details stay server-side).</li>\n<li><strong>Rate limiting</strong> on the API (per-client, per-endpoint windows). Behind the same-host Next.js proxy the client address comes from <code>X-Forwarded-For</code>, which is trusted only from a loopback peer, so clients get separate buckets and can't spoof their address by calling the API directly.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">Deployment</h2><a id=\"user-content-deployment\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Deployment\" href=\"#deployment\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The platform runs generated code in a <strong>Docker sandbox</strong>, so it needs a host with a real Docker daemon; managed PaaS free tiers that disallow Docker-in-Docker (Render/Railway) can't run the test stage. The included kit deploys the whole stack (API, web, Postgres, and the sandbox) onto <strong>one small AWS box</strong>, fully scripted and on-demand:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-shell notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"bash deploy/provision.sh        # launch + self-install an SSM-managed t4g.small (zero inbound ports)\nbash deploy/manage.sh url       # print the free Cloudflare tunnel URL once it's up\nbash deploy/manage.sh stop      # on-demand: stop when idle (billing drops to disk only)\nbash deploy/manage.sh backups   # list the nightly database backups in S3\nbash deploy/manage.sh teardown  # delete everything ($0)\"><pre>bash deploy/provision.sh        <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> launch + self-install an SSM-managed t4g.small (zero inbound ports)</span>\nbash deploy/manage.sh url       <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> print the free Cloudflare tunnel URL once it's up</span>\nbash deploy/manage.sh stop      <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> on-demand: stop when idle (billing drops to disk only)</span>\nbash deploy/manage.sh backups   <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> list the nightly database backups in S3</span>\nbash deploy/manage.sh teardown  <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> delete everything ($0)</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Postgres runs in a container, jobs run inline (no Redis), and the public URL is a free <code>*.trycloudflare.com</code> quick tunnel (no Cloudflare account, no open ports). The schema is applied with migrations, the API runs as compiled JavaScript, and the database is backed up nightly to a private S3 bucket (kept 30 days; restoring is in the runbook). The LLM stays off on the demo: registration is open, so a paid key there could be spent by anyone. Secrets (JWT signing key, database password) are generated at launch and never committed. Full runbook, costs, and the stable-URL upgrade: <a href=\"deploy/DEPLOY.md\"><code>deploy/DEPLOY.md</code></a>.</p>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">Operational notes</h2><a id=\"user-content-operational-notes\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Operational notes\" href=\"#operational-notes\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><strong>Jobs are opt-in durable.</strong> With no <code>REDIS_URL</code>, generation/test/repair run inline in-request, which is fine for dev and CI. Set <code>REDIS_URL</code> to route them through BullMQ so they survive restarts. Either way, a boot-time reconciler settles anything a crash stranded: a generation run still <code>running</code> after 5 min fails, and a project stuck mid-test (then <code>SANDBOX_FAILED</code>, safe to retry) or mid-repair (then <code>TESTS_FAILED</code>) after 15 min is recovered with an audit event, so the pipeline never hangs.</li>\n<li><strong>The repair loop runs on the queue.</strong> A clean test failure triggers up to <code>MAX_REPAIR_ATTEMPTS</code> passes (LLM fix → sandbox rerun). Only a fix whose rerun passes is saved; on exhaustion the project settles on <code>TESTS_FAILED</code> (never a silent success) with the generated code unchanged, and every attempt stays in the repair history. The user may still download that partial output: any download with warnings (tests failed, errored, or never ran; auth to configure) embeds a <code>WARNINGS.md</code> saying so.</li>\n<li><strong>The LLM is Claude, opt-in.</strong> Set <code>LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic</code> and <code>ANTHROPIC_API_KEY</code> in <code>apps/api/.env</code>; <code>ANTHROPIC_MODEL</code> picks the model (default Claude Haiku 4.5). Every call's tokens and estimated cost appear in the audit trail and in <code>/metrics</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Local storage for MVP.</strong> Artifacts are written under <code>STORAGE_DIR</code> (temp dir by default); the storage layer is abstracted so an object store can replace it without touching callers.</li>\n</ul>\n</article></div>";
